    284  f0ef							; --- E4 moth body (bank2 free space $F008-$F9D8) -------------------------
    285  f0ef							; Entered from bank0 via the $FEF0 entry tramp (sta $1FF8 lands on the
    286  f0ef							; jmp below at $FEF3). Exits via `jmp MothExitPad` ($FC49): bank2 runs
    287  f0ef							; sta $1FF6, bank0 serves jmp UE_Next. Rules:
    288  f0ef							;   - NEVER jsr FoldIndirect or any bank0 routine (a fold from inside
    289  f0ef							;     bank2 would switch away mid-routine = frozen player).
    290  f0ef							;   - Enemy records ARE here (org $F9D9) — read directly, no fold needed.
    291  f0ef							;   - Keep the whole routine inline (no jsr): tramps are tail jmps so
    292  f0ef							;     the stack depth equals the UE body (+0 vs the $F8 guard).
    293  f0ef							;   - ZP (rect cache, EnemyRam*, EnemyDataLo/Hi) is RAM: bank-independent.
    294  f100					      org	$F100
    295  f100				   MothRoutine
    296  f100							; E4 Stage C: horizontal patrol (docs/e4_moth_plan.md). 1 px / 2 frames
    297  f100							; (EnemyRamP & 1), range = spawn ± 8 tiles (32 px), wall/range/wrap =
    298  f100							; flip dir + hold, clear = commit candidate. Row/col inputs feed a
    299  f100							; verbatim copy of PlayerHitsMap's P3.4 rect walk; HIT turns instead of
    300  f100							; returning C=1.
    301  f100							; In: X = slot, Y = record base, FetchPtr = record base (records are in
    302  f100							; THIS bank — direct (FetchPtr),Y reads, NO fold). NEVER jsr bank0
    303  f100							; (mid-bank2 fold = frozen player). Slot is saved to EnemyIndex because
    304  f100							; the col swap and walk both use X (E3 lesson). Every exit re-stages
    305  f100							; FetchPtr (the walk overwrites it with window bytes) then
    306  f100							; jmp MothExitPad (sta $1FF6 / jmp UE_Next in bank0).
    307  f100		       a5 c2		      lda	EnemyRamP
    308  f102		       29 01		      and	#1
    309  f104		       f0 03		      beq	.MothRun	; branch-over-jmp (tail labels exceed ±127)
    310  f106		       4c 1a f2 	      jmp	MothExit	; ÷2 gate: 1 px / 2 frames
    311  f109				   .MothRun
    312  f109		       86 b9		      stx	EnemyIndex	; slot — turn/commit paths restore it
    313  f10b		       a5 c1		      lda	EnemyRamD	; live dir bit
    314  f10d		       3d 25 f2 	      and	MothBitTable,X
    315  f110		       d0 08		      bne	.MothR
    316  f112		       b5 bd		      lda	EnemyRamX,X
    317  f114		       38		      sec
